              "components": {
                "minecraft:written_book_content": {
                  "title": "Her Ledger",
                  "author": "unsigned",
                  "pages": [
                    "\"Third night of the thaw.\n\nThe wood is honest, whatever they say in the valley. It takes what it is owed and it warns you first. Thorns before teeth.\"",
                    "\"The children come as far as the stones and no further. Good. I have put nothing there to keep them out. Their own sense does it, and sense is cheaper than a fence.\"",
                    "\"Torches burn here. They simply do not help. I have watched a man stand inside his own lamplight and call out for someone to bring a light.\"",
                    "\"A flame the colour of the sky before dawn will hold. Nothing else will. I did not make that rule and I cannot unmake it.\"",
                    "\"If you are reading this, you have opened a chest in a house that is not yours, in a wood that is not yours, at an hour I would not have chosen.\n\nTake the bread. Leave the rest.\""
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
